    "revision": "v7 acting replacement",
    "status": "revised for review",
    "editMethod": "built-in image_gen; native alpha; uniform scale and separate lettering",
    "change": "Replace the old collapsed defeated pose with a comically flustered almost-trip while trying to catch ONE falling wooden spoon. Jango lunges diagonally forward with the rigid head/hat and compact torso leaning in the same direction. Both short arms reach forward from beneath the head, the two open pouch mittens are spaced apart ready to catch the spoon in midair just beyond them. One planted foot supports the weight and the other foot lifts behind for balance; torso stays compact, not stretched. The spoon is clearly separate, angled falling downward, with two tiny motion ticks. Eyes retain MASTER oval size and spacing, eyebrows rise unevenly, mouth is a small startled open oval. It should read as a small clumsy mistake, NOT sorrow or hopelessness. No old kneeling/crawling pose, no tears, no duplicate spoon. Full body and spoon visible.",
    "alphaExtrema": [
      0,
      255
    ],
    "title": "앗, 놓쳤다",
    "hasText": false,
    "changedInV7": true,
    "previousLine": "망했다",
    "changedInV8": false,
