    "editMethod": "built-in image_gen; native alpha; uniform scale and separate lettering",
    "change": "Replace the old seated crouch with a STANDING inward, emotionally hurt pose. Feet together, toes slightly inward, knees close. Head/hat and chest lower and tilt together gently, shoulders drawn inward while maintaining the same rigid proportions. One short arm raises a pouch mitten just below the mouth as if holding back a sob; the other short arm brings its mitten to firmly grip the LOWER apron hem at the hip, wrinkling only the fabric slightly. Eyes remain standard black ovals with sad inner brows, a tiny trembling mouth mostly visible above the mitten, and at most ONE small tear along one lower cheek. The whole contracted standing body must communicate holding back tears; the tear is secondary. No sitting, no table, no falling pose, no river of tears, no fist pump, no heart. Full body.",
