    "editMethod": "built-in image_gen; native alpha; uniform scale and separate lettering",
    "change": "Replace the old one-handed rice-ball offering with a welcoming invitation to eat a PROPER COOKED MEAL together. Jango takes one small step toward the viewer, connected head/hat and chest inclining forward. BOTH short mitten hands support the underside/edges of ONE white oval plate held horizontally at chest/apron level, distinctly below the mouth. On it is one clearly recognizable plump golden-yellow OMURICE (omelette over rice), warm yellow oval dome, three simple red ketchup stripes across the top. Plate approximately .60 head widths, omurice .43 head widths; hearty and readable at small size. Two restrained steam strokes above food. Hands must contact and support the plate naturally, thumb plus pouch only; do not fuse plate into the apron or head. Open welcoming small smile, bright normal MASTER oval eyes. The delicious meal is offered toward the other person, not eaten by Jango. No rice ball, separate rice bowl, lunchbox, spoon to mouth, extra dishes, table, tiny dessert cube, or elaborate garnish. Full body and whole plate. No lettering; Korean invitation will be added separately.",
